!!id:"https://tson.io/test-suite/class2/schema/valid/a-text-type-carries-a-member-set-expected.tn"
!!schema:"https://tson.io/test-suite/schemas/schema-sidecar.tn"
{
  spec: "[TSON-SCHEMA] §7.4, [TSON-SCHEMA] §5.7, [TSON-SCHEMA] §9"
  description: """
    `text_type.members` is the sparse case on the text tier, as `integer_type.members` is on the
    integer one -- a value set on a type whose other facets are also wanted, where the family's own
    parsing still applies. It is a plain field beside `pattern` rather than an alternative to it: a
    pattern is a value set when it is an alternation and a shape when it is not, nothing decides
    which, and beside a shape a member set composes exactly as a bound does.

    `nordic` is the narrowing that arrangement exists to keep. §5.6's atom refinement merges over the
    source's bound values, so the resolved body carries the inherited `pattern` and the new
    `members` together, and every member answers to the pattern or the schema fails to load.

    Each of the pair is settable once: `nordic` could not have replaced the pattern, and nothing may
    shrink its member set afterwards. They occupy one logical position, and the pattern half cannot
    be narrowed without deciding regular-language containment, so the position takes one rule rather
    than two.
    """
  meta: "meta.tn"
  import: ["core.tn"]
  valid: {
    resolved: """
      !schema {
        country_code => !type_definition {
          source: text_type
          supertypes: [text]
          subtypes: [nordic]
          body: !text_type { pattern: "[A-Z]{2}" }
        }

        nordic => !type_definition {
          source: text_type
          supertypes: [country_code]
          body: !text_type { pattern: "[A-Z]{2}"  members: ["SE" "NO" "DK"] }
        }
      }
      """
  }
}
